@startuml h_holds
!include _style.puml
title H0 / H1 — holds with expiry, and the late payment

participant "Buyer A" as A
participant "Database" as DB
participant "Sweeper" as S
participant "Buyer B" as B

A -> DB : hold: UPDATE event SET seats_taken+1 WHERE seats_taken < capacity\nINSERT reservation (held, expires in 250 ms)
A -> DB : pre-payment check: held AND not expired?  → true
activate A
note over A : paying… (card authorisation takes longer than the hold has left)
S -> DB : expired holds FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED\nUPDATE reservation SET released WHERE status='held'\nUPDATE event SET seats_taken−1
B -> DB : hold: the released seat → granted
B -> DB : confirm → ticket issued
deactivate A

alt H0 — naive confirm (NEGATIVE CONTROL)
  A -> DB : UPDATE reservation SET status='confirmed' WHERE reservation_id=$\nINSERT ticket
  DB --> A : 1 row — **the same seat is now sold twice**
else H1 — checked confirm
  A -> DB : UPDATE reservation SET status='confirmed'\n WHERE reservation_id=$ AND status='held' AND expires_at > now()
  DB --> A : 0 rows — refund, no ticket
end

note over DB
  The pre-payment check is identical in H0 and H1 and was TRUE when it ran.
  The only difference between the designs is the WHERE clause of the confirmation,
  evaluated by the database clock in the same statement that confirms.
end note
@enduml
